!Sample_source_name_ch1 = human pancreas FFPE
!Sample_organism_ch1 = Homo sapiens
!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: pancreas
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = sample preparation: human FFPE tissue
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = input: 10 mm ^2, 5 micron thick
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = For preparing FFPE cell pellets, live cells were washed twice with 1X PBS, and then fixed with 1% formaldehyde in 1X PBS for 30 minutes at room temperature
!Sample_growth_protocol_ch1 = For experiments involving cell pellets, MCF7 and MDA-MB-231 cells were grown in RPMI supplemented with 10% FBS
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = For cells that were not prepared as FFPE, cells were washed once with PBS, then lysed using TempO-Seq Lysis Buffer
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = TempO-Seq targeted expression assay. Addition of adapters by amplification.
!Sample_description = HumanGeneCountsMaster.csv
!Sample_description = F2pan1
!Sample_data_processing = base calling on instrument with RTA
!Sample_data_processing = no adapter trimming for TempO-Seq fastqs, default settings for clusters passing filters
!Sample_data_processing = then bcl2fastq v2.17.1.14 or v2.18.0.12 for demultiplexing and generating fastqs
!Sample_data_processing = fastqs were aligned to a pseudo transcriptome using Bowtie, allowing up to 2 mis-matches.
!Sample_data_processing = Genome_build: TempO-Seq is a targeted sequencing assay, and sequencing results are aligned to a pseudo-transcriptome formed from known probe sequences (see Yeakley et al., PLoS One. 2017, 12(5):e0178302). For each species, the entire pseudo-transcriptome used for alignment is present in the corresponding master gene count files (Probe_ID and Probe_Sequence columns).
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary_files_format_and_content: Probe_ID (genes) in column 1, Probe_Sequence used for alignment in column 2, Accession Number in column 3. Sample Names in row 1.
